Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:01:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/26] pipeline: simple: Support the MediaTek MT6878 CAMSV

The MT6878 (Dimensity 7300) CAMSV engine is a raw capture DMA behind the
SENINF CSI-2 receiver. With the mainline CAMSV driver (mtk-camsv-mt6878),
every CAMSV instance is a media device, driver name "mtk-camsv" (the
media_device_info driver field holds 15 characters), with one chain

  sensor -> mtk-seninf-mt6878 (subdev) -> CAMSV (video node)

and the video node delivers raw Bayer frames (CSI-2 packed RAW10 among
others). There is no ISP on this path, so enable the software ISP.

Used on the Unihertz Titan 2 (Hi-847, IMX766, S5KGD1SP sensors).

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index c6fe12d..0566423 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -261,6 +261,7 @@ static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "intel-ipu6", {}, true },
 	{ "intel-ipu7", {}, true },
 	{ "j721e-csi2rx", {}, true },
+	{ "mtk-camsv", {}, true },
 	{ "mtk-seninf", { { "mtk-mdp", 3 } }, false },
 	{ "mxc-isi", {}, false },
 	{ "qcom-camss", {}, true },
